**Reasoning:**
1. **Two orderings**: Light-first and heavy-first greedy produce different placements; picking the best of the two hedges against bad orderings at ~2x the (tiny) greedy cost.
2. **Local search refinement**: The greedy pass can leave the worst GPU overloaded; moving a single model off it directly targets the objective (minimize max KVPR). Prior attempts showed this reduces max KVPR significantly.
3. **Simplicity**: Only a move-based pass (no swaps), keeping runtime well under a millisecond on typical test sizes, so the combined score gain comes almost entirely from the max_kvpr reduction.
